Add first-run onboarding wizard

Replace the bare "jump to Settings" first run with a guided wizard that mirrors
the macOS setup flow, built as a thin shell over the tested Core SetupWizard
state machine:

- Steps: Welcome, provider connection (endpoint/key/model/version), shortcut
  overview, microphone acknowledgement, finish — Next/Finish gated by the same
  SetupWizard.IsStepComplete rules asserted in the inner loop.
- Persists a GeneralSettings.HasCompletedOnboarding flag; the wizard only shows
  when unset AND no transcription credentials exist, so configured users
  upgrading from an earlier build are not sent back through it.
- On finish the app saves settings and restarts so the entered provider
  credentials are wired into the pipeline; "Skip for now" records completion and
  enters the app.

Inner loop GREEN at 197; app builds x86 clean; portable smoke test launches
without crashing.

